<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Guangwu of Han</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5 BCE–57 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Liu Xiu, Emperor Guangwu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Guangwu of Han, born Liu Xiu, was a descendant of the Han imperial house who rose against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-mang">Wang Mang</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xin-dynasty">Xin dynasty</a> and restored the Han in 25 CE, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Eastern Han</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>. He reunified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> by 36, conquering the Chengjia state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a>, and received envoys from distant lands such as the Japanese state of Na.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-guangwu-of-han.jpg" alt="Emperor Guangwu of Han" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yan Li-pen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Han_Guangwu_Di.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The golden seal that <b>Emperor Guangwu</b> of the Later Han dynasty gave to the Na state of Wo in 57 CE, recorded in the Book of the Later Han, was found in northern Kyushu in the 18th century.</blockquote><a href="/culture/yayoi-culture">Yayoi culture · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Emperor Guangwu of Han</b>, who had risen against Wang Mang's Xin dynasty and restored the Han, declared Luoyang the capital of the Eastern Han dynasty.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-27">27 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>His death cleared the way for the restoration of the Han dynasty under <b>Emperor Guangwu</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-6">6 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>As the Xin collapsed he seized the region, took the title King of Shu and in 25 proclaimed himself emperor of Chengjia, with his capital at Chengdu, the same year <b>Liu Xiu</b> restored the Han.</blockquote><a href="/state/chengjia">Chengjia</a></li><li><blockquote>The Book of the Later Han records that its king sent envoys to <b>Emperor Guangwu</b> in 57 and received a seal; a gold seal reading King of Na of Wa of Han was found on Shikanoshima island in 1784.</blockquote><a href="/state/na-japan">Na (Japan)</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Liu Xiu</b>, a Han kinsman, restored the dynasty in 25 as Emperor Guangwu, beginning the Eastern Han.</blockquote><a href="/state/xin-dynasty">Xin dynasty</a></li></ul></section>
